Zoe: Quick note — I'm consolidating the SDK snippets for streaming + pagination across py/ts/go. Opened PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1337
Arjun: Thanks. Tests flagged: missing include (includes/old_stream_example.md) and TS using deprecated helper.
Marta: Agreed we should standardize on client.responses.paginate() + client.responses.stream(). Use for-await-of for TS, sync/async examples for Python, and a small helper for Go.
Zoe: Draft Python sync snippet (tiny):
```
from redwood import Redwood
import time, random
client = Redwood()

def retry(fn, tries=3):
  for i in range(tries):
    try:
      return fn()
    except Exception:
      time.sleep(min(2**i + random.random(), 6))
  raise

for page in client.responses.paginate(model='rw-small', page_size=2):
  for chunk in client.responses.stream(page.cursor):
    print(getattr(chunk, 'text', '') or getattr(chunk, 'delta', ''))

# safe create with idempotency key
resp = retry(lambda: client.responses.create(model='rw-small', input='hi', idempotency_key='op-99'))
print(resp)
```
Arjun: TS snippet:```
for await (const page of client.responses.paginate({ model: 'rw-small', page_size: 2 })) {
  for await (const part of client.responses.stream(page.cursor)) {
    console.log(part.delta ?? part.text)
  }
}
```
Marta: Go main doc should call StreamWithPagination helper defined in includes so readers don't handle cursor details:```
ch := StreamWithPagination(client, "rw-small", 2)
for chunk := range ch {
  fmt.Println(chunk.Text)
}
```
